// One tool call from an external MCP client. Render as: sequence-diagram
typeface clean
autoNumber on

Client [icon: terminal, color: gray, label: "MCP client"]
Traefik [icon: traefik, color: blue]
Gateway [icon: node, color: purple]
Postgres [icon: postgres, color: purple]
WooMcp [icon: node, color: green, label: "woo-mcp"]
Woo [icon: woocommerce, color: green, label: "WooCommerce"]

Client > Traefik: tools/call woo__list_orders, with the user's API key
Traefik > Gateway: forward /mcp
activate Gateway
Gateway > Postgres: look up the key: hash matches, not revoked, user active
Gateway > Gateway: split the name into server "woo" and tool "list_orders", check role policy
alt [label: woo-mcp answers in time, color: green] {
  Gateway > WooMcp: tools/call list_orders, with the gateway's own token for woo-mcp
  activate WooMcp
  WooMcp > Woo: GET /wp-json/wc/v3/orders, OAuth 1.0a signature (secret never sent)
  Woo --> WooMcp: orders
  WooMcp --> Gateway: tool result
  deactivate WooMcp
}
else [label: timeout or unreachable, color: red] {
  Gateway > Gateway: build a clear error, e.g. "WooCommerce did not respond within 30s"
}
Gateway > Postgres: write the audit row: user, server, tool, duration, outcome
Gateway --> Traefik: result
deactivate Gateway
Traefik --> Client: result
